[00:24.34]1. O God, you know my rest and waking,
[00:31.44]When I lie down and when I rise anew.
[00:38.52]You search my thoughts, my inmost inclination,
[00:46.18]The words I speak, the ways I walk,
[00:50.64]you know them too.
[00:55.30]You saw when I was made in secret,
[01:01.56]My very bones not hidden from your sight.
[01:09.08]You saw my form; its parts were down in writing.
[01:17.42]I love the wonder of your ways
[01:21.04]and praise your might.
[01:25.08]Your knowledge, God, is wondrous, awe-inspiring;
[01:32.12]Of this my soul is very well-aware.
[01:40.06]If I should fear that darkness might enfold me,
[01:47.66]Your spirit, God, would find me, even there.
[01:55.24]Where could I hide from you, Jehovah,
[02:02.64]Or be concealed, be hidden from your face?
[02:09.74]Not in the Grave nor in the highest heaven,
[02:17.20]Not in the dark nor in the sea;
[02:21.18]there is no place.
